WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.639 --> 00:00:03.556
(crowd chattering)

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:09.450
- [Narrator] Social media
footage shows crowds protesting

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:10.630
in front of the offices

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:13.800
of the Chinese real estate
developer Evergrande.

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:17.880
- Evergrande is one of China's
biggest property developers.

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:20.200
It has the biggest sales

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.980
in terms of property sales in China.

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:25.070
- [Narrator] In recent days,
security has been stepped up

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:27.820
outside its headquarters
as the struggling company

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:30.130
faces complaints from small investors,

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:32.830
unpaid suppliers and people
unhappy that the homes

00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:35.510
that they purchase haven't
yet been completed.

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:39.260
In total, Evergrande owes
more than $300 billion.

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:41.843
- It's one of the most indebted
companies in the world.

00:00:43.147 --> 00:00:43.980
Evergrande borrowed a lot of money,

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:47.300
what we call offshore in
international financial markets,

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:49.280
and it's probably not gonna pay it back.

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:50.900
- [Narrator] Evergrande's
massive debt problem

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:54.330
has rippled out into global
markets with the S&amp;P 500

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:56.250
seeing big swings.

00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:58.670
Beyond the potential default,
international investors

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:01.320
are particularly worried
about what may happen next

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:04.800
as a big chunk of China's
economy is linked to real estate.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:07.870
- If Evergrande fails and drags down

00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:12.530
the whole property sector,
people worry if Chinese economy

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:17.530
could develop at high speed
as it did in the past years.

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:19.810
- [Narrator] More bullish
investors think China

00:01:19.810 --> 00:01:21.870
could find a way to contain the fallout,

00:01:21.870 --> 00:01:23.500
but others are less certain

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:25.840
that this can be safely diffused.

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:28.250
This one company has got markets on edge,

00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:30.720
and it struggles could
have big repercussions

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:32.710
for global investors.

00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:36.330
- In recent months,
Evergrande has been caught

00:01:36.330 --> 00:01:40.040
into one of the largest
crisis in its history.

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:42.460
- [Narrator] For years, Evergrande
raised a lot of its cash

00:01:42.460 --> 00:01:45.520
by borrowing billions of dollars
from banks and investors,

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:47.450
and pre-selling unfinished apartments

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:50.030
so that it could amass more
land and develop projects

00:01:50.030 --> 00:01:52.700
in over 200 Chinese cities.

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:55.700
It has some 800 projects underway.

00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:59.130
But this year, its shares have
lost about 80% of their value

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:01.100
in just a few months.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:03.730
Problems started for the
company when pandemic lockdowns

00:02:03.730 --> 00:02:06.430
hurt property sales, and
when Chinese authorities

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:08.920
said they wanted to fight
speculation in real estate

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:10.870
and announced rules that barred Evergrande

00:02:10.870 --> 00:02:12.110
from taking on new debt.

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:15.090
- Many of its construction projects

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:18.160
all over China has stopped.

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:21.880
It started to face mounting
pressure, complaints,

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:26.560
and protests from suppliers,
contractors, home buyers,

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:29.450
and small investors all over the country.

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:31.560
- [Narrator] In this footage
from Chinese social media,

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:34.210
people can be seen
asking for compensation.

00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:35.710
The Wall Street Journal couldn't determine

00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:37.850
the author of the video or the exact date

00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:39.570
of this particular protest,

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:42.200
and this clip has since been taken down.

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:44.070
These photos show small investors

00:02:44.070 --> 00:02:46.780
being surrounded by security
as they tried to enter

00:02:46.780 --> 00:02:49.740
the company's headquarters in Shenzhen.

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:51.820
Evergrande has repeatedly
said that it would try

00:02:51.820 --> 00:02:54.303
to reimburse people and
resume construction.

00:02:55.370 --> 00:02:57.530
Evergrande's struggles
are raising questions

00:02:57.530 --> 00:02:59.490
over China's property market.

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:01.950
- Evergrande is such a big player

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:04.860
on China's property industry.

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:09.640
The property industry
account for about 25%

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:12.610
of the total economy.

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:17.170
So, if growth in that sector is eroded,

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:21.710
we will see the macro
economy under big challenges.

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:23.533
- [Narrator] In a memo on September 21st,

00:03:23.533 --> 00:03:25.490
Evergrande's chairman
acknowledged the issues

00:03:25.490 --> 00:03:29.260
that the company faces, but
vowed to push through the pain.

00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:31.960
Wall Street Journal reporting
found that Chinese authorities

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:33.220
have asked local governments

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:36.120
to contain the potential
downfall of Evergrande.

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:39.070
But the government has been
reluctant to bail it out,

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:41.340
and global investors are watching to see

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:43.920
how this could affect
this year's market rally.

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:46.900
- The stock market has gone
up a ton since the pandemic

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:49.650
especially in the US, and
there's this sense of,

00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:53.480
what can make things go higher
and what could go wrong?

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:55.530
- [Narrator] Some investors
think letting Evergrande fail

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:57.360
would be a sign that China is serious

00:03:57.360 --> 00:03:59.250
about reducing debt in the economy.

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:01.800
- People we talked to widely believe

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:05.810
Beijing won't step in
to protect shareholders

00:04:05.810 --> 00:04:10.810
or bond holders this time, but
they might take some actions

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:14.300
if they see social arrest spread,

00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:17.160
or if they see financial markets

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:21.158
being roid heavily by Evergrande.

00:04:21.158 --> 00:04:23.741
(upbeat music)

